BLAISENOTEBOOK OPEN SOURCE DUAL LICENSE AGREEMENT
================================================================================

BlaiseNotebook is open-source software and follows the standard Lazarus /
Free Pascal / BlaiseVue licensing model:

- The BlaiseNotebook Kernel / CLI Tools & Server Executables:
  Licensed under the GNU General Public License v2 (GNU GPL v2).

- The BlaiseNotebook Core Libraries, Components & Scientific Runtime:
  Licensed under the Modified GNU LGPL v2.1 with a Static Linking Exception.

STATIC LINKING EXCEPTION:
As a special exception, the copyright holders of this library give you
permission to link this library with independent modules to produce an
executable, regardless of the license terms of these independent modules,
and to copy and distribute the resulting executable under terms of your choice,
provided that you also meet, for each linked independent module, the terms
and conditions of the license of that module. An independent module is a
module which is not derived from or based on this library. If you modify
this library, you may extend this exception to your version of the library,
but you are not obligated to do so. If you do not wish to do so, delete this
exception statement from your version.

This allows developers, scientists, and engineers to build proprietary models,
data science pipelines, and commercial applications without having to open-source
their private business logic or scientific algorithms, while ensuring the
BlaiseNotebook platform and runtime remain open and accessible to all.

